#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:295
msgid "Installation & activation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:300
msgid "Go to <strong>Plugins → Add New</strong>, search for “Accessi Compliance Kit”, click <strong>Install Now</strong>, then <strong>Activate</strong>. (Or upload the zip via <strong>Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin</strong>.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:301
msgid "On activation the plugin creates one database table for scan results and seeds its default settings. <strong>All fixes start OFF</strong> — activating changes nothing on your store’s front end."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:302
msgid "Find the plugin under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:308
msgid "Recommended first-run flow"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:313
msgid "Run a scan of your home page from the <strong>Scan</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:314
msgid "Review the detected issues, starting with Critical and Serious."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:315
msgid "Enable one fix at a time in <strong>Settings</strong>, then spot-check your store."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:316
msgid "Generate the accessibility statement draft and edit it before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:317
msgid "Re-scan regularly — or turn on the weekly email reminder."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:325
msgid "Running a Scan"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:328
msgid "Scan from the admin page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:333
msgid "Open <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and go to the <strong>Scan</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:334
msgid "The URL field is pre-filled with your home page; paste any URL <strong>on your own site</strong> (other domains are rejected by design)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:335
msgid "Click <strong>Scan this page</strong>. The page loads in a hidden frame and is checked in your browser by the bundled axe-core engine — nothing is sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:336
msgid "Results appear grouped by severity. Expand a row to see the affected element’s HTML, the CSS selector, why it was flagged, and a link to remediation guidance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:342
msgid "Scan from the front end"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:346
msgid "While browsing your store logged in as an admin, click <strong>Scan this page</strong> in the admin bar — it opens the Scan tab with the current URL pre-filled."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:351
msgid "Scan history"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:355
msgid "The <strong>History</strong> tab lists past scans (date, URL, status, per-severity counts). Click a row to reopen its full results. Results are stored in your own database and never leave your server."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:362
msgid "Understanding Results"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:365
msgid "The four severity levels"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:370
msgid "<strong>Critical</strong> — blocks some users completely (e.g. an image conveying information with no text alternative)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:371
msgid "<strong>Serious</strong> — makes a core task very difficult (e.g. form fields without labels)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:372
msgid "<strong>Moderate</strong> — causes real friction but usually has a workaround."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:373
msgid "<strong>Minor</strong> — polish-level problems still worth cleaning up."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:378
msgid "Work top-down: clear Critical and Serious issues first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:383
msgid "Why “detected issues” and not “violations”?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:387
msgid "Automated results always include findings that need human interpretation — for example contrast on decorative elements, or alternative text that exists but is unhelpful. We report what the engine detected and leave the judgment to you."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:392
msgid "What automated scans can and cannot find"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:396
msgid "Automated checkers — including the industry-standard axe-core engine this plugin bundles — reliably detect roughly a third to a half of WCAG issues. The rest (keyboard flows, meaningful alt text, content clarity, sensible focus order) need human judgment. Treat a clean scan as a good baseline, not proof of compliance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:403
msgid "The Six Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:404
msgid "Enable each fix under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility → Settings</strong>. Each is independent, off by default, and instant to switch off again. Recommended: enable one at a time and re-check your store."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:408
#: src/Statement/StatementGenerator.php:131
msgid "Accessibility Statement"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:411
msgid "Create the statement page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:416
msgid "Go to <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and find the <strong>Accessibility Statement</strong> card."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:417
msgid "Click <strong>Create statement page</strong>. A WordPress page titled “Accessibility Statement” is created from an EAA-oriented English template, pre-filled with your site name, contact details, and the current date."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:418
msgid "If a statement page already exists, the plugin warns you instead of creating a duplicate; creating a fresh page is an explicit second action."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:424
msgid "Edit before you publish"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:428
msgid "Treat the generated page as a strong draft, not a finished statement. It contains placeholders — notably the compliance level you claim and the “known limitations” section — that only you can fill in truthfully."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:433
msgid "Where to link it"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:437
msgid "Link the published page from your site footer — most stores put it next to the privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:444
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:447
msgid "Dashboard widget & admin-bar notice"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:451
msgid "The WordPress dashboard widget shows your last scan date and detected-issue counts by severity, with a link to the full results. An admin-bar notice appears when your most recent scan detected critical issues."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:456
msgid "Weekly email reminder (opt-in)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:460
msgid "Enable it in <strong>Settings</strong> to get a weekly email nudging you to re-scan. It uses WP-Cron and your site’s normal mail configuration; no external service is involved."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:467
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:470
msgid "The scan times out or never finishes"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:474
msgid "The scanned page must load in an iframe from your own site. Security plugins or headers that block same-origin framing (<code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code>, a strict <code>frame-ancestors</code> CSP) will prevent the scan — allow same-origin framing and retry. Scans also require you to be logged in as an admin; a scan fails if the URL redirects (e.g. to a login page)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:479
msgid "“This URL is not part of this site.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:483
msgid "By design the scanner only accepts URLs on your own domain. Check for a different subdomain, protocol, or a trailing typo."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:488
msgid "The menu item is missing"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:492
msgid "The plugin registers nothing until WooCommerce 8.0+ is active — check the Plugins screen for WooCommerce. The menu lives under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and requires an administrator account."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:497
msgid "A fix doesn’t seem to do anything"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:501
msgid "Most fixes are invisible by design (screen-reader text, <code>alt</code>/<code>aria</code> attributes). Verify with your browser’s element inspector, or re-run a scan of the same page and compare detected-issue counts. Also check for full-page caching — purge the cache after toggling a fix."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:506
msgid "The scan reports issues from my theme or page builder"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:510
msgid "The scanner reports everything on the rendered page regardless of origin. The per-issue guidance describes what needs to change; changes to theme markup need to happen in the theme (or a child theme), not in this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:517
msgid "Privacy & Data"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:520
msgid "What the plugin stores — and what leaves your site"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:524
msgid "Zero external calls. The axe-core engine ships inside the plugin, scans run in your browser, and results live in your database. No telemetry, no CDN, no accounts, no API keys."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:529
msgid "Scan results (one database table)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:530
msgid "The plugin’s settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:531
msgid "The ID of the generated statement page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:537
msgid "Deactivating vs. deleting"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:541
msgid "Deactivating keeps your data. <strong>Deleting</strong> the plugin via the Plugins screen removes the scans table and all plugin options. The generated Accessibility Statement page is a normal WordPress page and is never deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:548
msgid "For Developers"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:551
msgid "Prefixes, body classes & data"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:556
msgid "All AJAX actions, options, hooks, CSS classes, and script handles are prefixed <code>accessi_compliance_kit_</code> / <code>.accessi-compliance-kit-</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:557
msgid "When any fix is active, <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> gets the class <code>accessi-compliance-kit-fixes-active</code> plus one class per active fix — use these to scope your own CSS overrides."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:558
msgid "Scan results live in the <code>accessi_compliance_kit_scans</code> table (with your site’s table prefix); treat it as read-only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:559
msgid "Source JS is included under <code>assets/js/src/</code>; builds use <code>@wordpress/scripts</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:567
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:598
msgid "Will the fixes change my design or slow my store?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:602
msgid "Only “Visible focus states” has any visual effect — a high-contrast outline shown when an element is focused with the keyboard, which is exactly what WCAG requires. Performance impact is negligible: most fixes are PHP filters, and the rest load one small CSS/JS file only while enabled. No external requests, ever."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:608
msgid "If a fix conflicts with your theme"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: WordPress.org support forum URL.
#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:614
msgid "Switch it off — the change is removed immediately — and report the theme + fix combination in the <a href=\"%s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">support forum</a> so we can improve compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:633
msgid "Does this plugin make my store legally compliant with the EAA or ADA?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:638
msgid "No automated tool can, and you should distrust any that claims to. This plugin gives you an honest starting point: detected issues to review, opt-in fixes for common WooCommerce problems, and a statement template. It is not legal advice."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:643
msgid "Does the European Accessibility Act apply to my store?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:647
msgid "The EAA has been enforceable across all 27 EU member states since June 28, 2025. It generally applies to e-commerce sites selling to EU consumers and requires WCAG 2.1 Level AA. Micro-enterprises are exempt: fewer than 10 employees <strong>and</strong> annual turnover under €2M. Whether it applies to you specifically is a legal question — ask a professional."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:652
msgid "Is this an accessibility overlay like UserWay or accessiBe?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:656
msgid "No. Overlays add a floating toolbar and scripts that mask problems without fixing the page; disability advocates and European regulators consider them inadequate. This plugin reports real issues in your markup and, only when you opt in, fixes the actual markup."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:661
msgid "Does any data leave my site? Do I need an account?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:665
msgid "No and no. The scan engine is bundled in the plugin, scans run in your own browser against your own pages, and results are stored in your own WordPress database. The free version makes zero external requests."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:670
msgid "Do I need WooCommerce? Which versions are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:674
msgid "Yes — the plugin targets WooCommerce stores specifically. Requirements: WordPress 6.5+, WooCommerce 8.0+, PHP 7.4+."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:679
msgid "Why are all six fixes off by default?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:683
msgid "Because every theme is different and we never alter your store without explicit opt-in. Recommended flow: run a scan, enable one fix, spot-check your store, repeat. Each fix switches off just as instantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:688
msgid "What happens to my data if I remove the plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:692
msgid "Deactivating keeps everything. Deleting the plugin from the Plugins screen removes the plugin’s database table and options. The generated Accessibility Statement page is a normal WordPress page and is never deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:697
msgid "Is there a Pro version?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/GuidePage.php:701
msgid "Not yet. The free version is complete on its own. A Pro tier (full-site crawling, scheduled scans, PDF audit reports, advanced WooCommerce fixes) is planned post-launch."
msgstr ""

